From: MedyMa <75345465+MedyMa@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: mediatek: release RX buffers with a zero low DMA address

DMA address zero is valid, and a 36-bit address such as 0x100000000 also
has a zero rxd1. Do not use that register as the allocation sentinel.
ring->data is assigned only after successful buffer allocation and DMA
mapping, and already guards the cleanup loop. Use that ownership record
so plain mappings and Page Pool buffers are both released at this boundary.

Signed-off-by: MedyMa <75345465+MedyMa@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -3635,9 +3635,6 @@
 				continue;
 
 			rxd = ring->dma + i * eth->soc->rx.desc_size;
-			if (!rxd->rxd1)
-				continue;
-
 			if (MTK_HAS_CAPS(eth->soc->caps, MTK_36BIT_DMA))
 				addr64 = RX_DMA_GET_ADDR64(rxd->rxd2);
 
